From fa921407743ec658e6f799200530a715afde0e51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 06:53:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fill in the WinForms members the dialogs, Form, ComboBox and
 TreeNode lack

A WinForms program compiled against this library failed on members the
real one has:

- FontDialog: ShowEffects, ShowColor, ShowApply, FixedPitchOnly,
  FontMustExist, AllowVectorFonts, AllowSimulations, AllowScriptChange,
  Color, MinSize, MaxSize. GTK's font chooser has no counterpart for the
  chrome flags, so they carry the caller's choice as AllowFullOpen
  already does, and Reset restores the WinForms defaults.
- SaveFileDialog: OverwritePrompt, CreatePrompt. GTK's save chooser
  confirms an overwrite itself; the properties are here to be read back.
- Form.ActiveForm: the toplevel the window manager gives the keyboard to.
- Control.FromHandle: every control records itself on its widget, so the
  handle can be mapped back.
- ComboBox.BeginUpdate/EndUpdate, as on ListBox.
- TreeNode.TreeView is public, as in WinForms, and TreeNodeCollection
  gains Find(key, searchAllChildren) beside List<T>.Find(Predicate<T>).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
